course: dictionary
lesson: 11585
title: The word part anti-
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some word parts go at the front of a word and change its meaning. Anti- is one of them. It means against or opposite. Anticlockwise means going against the way a clock's hands turn.
explain: «The villagers were anti the new road, because it would go past their school.» Anti means against. The villagers did not want the road, so they were against it. Look at the words around the word to check.
explain: When you meet anti- at the start of a word, cover it up and read the rest. Antisocial: social means friendly with other people, so antisocial means not friendly with others. Put your meaning into the sentence and see if it makes sense.
explain: Anti can also stand alone in chatty talk: «She is an anti of the plan.» That means she is someone who is against the plan. It is informal, so use it carefully in school writing.
fact: Anti- is a prefix, a word part added to the front of a word.
fact: Anti- means against or opposite.
fact: «Anticlockwise» means in the opposite direction to the hands of a clock.
fact: «Antibiotic» is a medicine that works against germs (bacteria).
fact: On its own, «anti» is a preposition meaning against, and it is informal.
exercise: «Turn the tap anticlockwise to open it.» What does anticlockwise mean? | Up and down | In the same direction as a clock's hands | Very fast | *Against the way a clock's hands turn
exercise: The school has an anti-bullying week. What does anti- mean in anti-bullying? | Before bullying | Full of bullying | Bullying again | *Against bullying
exercise: Dad says the car has antifreeze in it. What does anti- mean in antifreeze? | *Against freezing | Freezing again | Frozen solid | Very cold
test: «Antibiotics help the doctor fight germs.» What does anti- mean in antibiotic? | Again | *Against | Under | Big
test: «The children wore anti-slip shoes so they would not fall on the wet floor.» What does anti-slip mean? | Very slippery | Made of wood | *Stops you slipping | Full of water
exam: Which sentence uses anti on its own, meaning against? | *The club was anti the plan from the start | Her anti shoes were red and new | Stop being antisocial at lunch | They walked anticlockwise round the park
